  "problem_statement": "RIOT's socket utility must parse URLs whose scheme has a length other than the short http case, including schemes such as https://. In particular, when given a URL with such a scheme and a host/port part that is too long, the parser must still produce the expected result for the overlong host/port case rather than misparsing the URL. Today such URLs are not handled correctly, and the too-long host/port condition can be missed when the scheme is https://.",
